// Fixture for the `attach`/`spec` interchange coverage in
// tests/integration/test_cli_surface.py (IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md Task 5.4,
// SPEC.md Sec 9.3's sibling CLI-surface requirements).
//
// Deliberately minimal and NOT reused from model/: every canonical model in
// this showcase (Patient, Appointment, Invoice, ...) uses at least one of
// uuid(N), enum(...), semantic-type refs, json, or binary(N) - and every one
// of those loses precision round-tripping through dbt's `schema.yml` type
// vocabulary (data_type: text/integer/numeric/timestamp/... has no way to
// express "uuid version 7", an enum's closed value set, or a named semantic
// type). Verified directly: attaching model/patient.mdl's own
// `compile --target dbt-yaml` output for Patient@2 back onto Patient@2
// always produces spurious drift (patientId's `uuid(7)` round-trips as a
// bare `Unknown`/`text`-derived type, enum fields round-trip as plain
// `string`, etc.) - real, structural lossiness in dbt's type system, not a
// Modelable bug, and not useful for demonstrating a genuine "no drift"
// result.
//
// This fixture uses only string/int/timestamp fields, the one type
// vocabulary subset that round-trips through dbt-yaml losslessly - verified
// empirically before being used as the "clean" half of the attach/spec
// tests. See test_cli_surface.py for the additive/breaking mutated
// counterparts.
domain importroundtrip {
  owner: "conformance-fixtures"

  entity Widget @ 1 (additive) {
    @key
    widgetId: string

    name: string
    quantity: int
    createdAt: timestamp
  }
}
